    {
      "id": "node_16",
      "name": "Assemble Prompt",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        2920,
        400
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "\nconst row = $json;\nconst cfg = row._config || $('Set Config Variables').first().json;\nconst prompt = `You are a social media content writer for Carematix, a healthcare technology company.\nCore message: Scale care with data, not staff.\nTone: Clear, confident, human, data-informed.\nBrand personality: Trustworthy, practical, forward-thinking, accessible.\nKey differentiators:\n- Cellular-First: No app, no Bluetooth, no home internet required\n- FDA-cleared device manufacturer, not importer or reseller\n- Scale Without Staff: Manage 1000 patients without adding 10 FTEs\n- Reimbursement-aligned: RPM 99453/99454, APCM G0557/G0558\n- Works where others fail: rural, elderly, low-tech, limited connectivity environments\n\nNEVER use these phrases in any output: improving patient engagement, revolutionary, game-changer, best-in-class, industry-leading, generic RPM definitions, feature-heavy posts without outcomes.\nNEVER make unsupported clinical claims.\nNEVER mention competitors (ThoroughCare, Prevounce, Tenovi) directly.\nNEVER give patient-specific medical advice.\nALWAYS use active voice.\nALWAYS be direct and get to the point in the first sentence.\nALWAYS tie features to a real outcome or business impact.\n\nLinkedIn: ${cfg.linkedin_word_range} words, professional B2B tone.\nRequired LinkedIn hashtags: #RPM #APCM #RemotePatientMonitoring #CareManagement #HealthcareLeaders\n\nFacebook: ${cfg.facebook_word_range} words, simple and human tone.\nRequired Facebook hashtags: #HeartHealth #DiabetesAwareness #RPM #Carematix\n\nInstagram: ${cfg.instagram_caption_length} words, short and punchy.\nRequired Instagram hashtags: #RPM #Carematix #RemotePatientMonitoring #HealthTech #ChronicCare\n\nAPPROVED SAMPLE POSTS (style reference only — do not copy):\nLinkedIn example 1: Care plans are important. But without real patient data, they are still reactive. RPM turns care management into something continuous and actionable.\nLinkedIn example 2: RPM does not fail because of technology. It fails because patients cannot use it. That is why connectivity has to be invisible.\nInstagram example: Data is only the first step. What matters is what happens next. RPM should drive action — not just dashboards.\n\nNow write content for the following row:\nProduct Education: ${row['Product Education']}\nContent Pillar: ${row['Content Pillar']}\nObjective: ${row['Objective']}\nAudience: ${row['Audience']}\nSuggested CTA: ${row['CTA']}\n\nReturn your response in this EXACT JSON format with no text outside the JSON block:\n{\n  \"linkedin_draft\": \"...\",\n  \"facebook_draft\": \"...\",\n  \"instagram_caption\": \"...\",\n  \"image_brief\": \"Brief description of what the Canva visual should show for this post\",\n  \"suggested_cta\": \"...\"\n}`;\nreturn {json: {...row, _prompt: prompt, _temperature: cfg.temperature, _gemini_model: cfg.gemini_model, _openrouter_model: cfg.openrouter_model}};\n",
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "node_17",
      "name": "Call Gemini",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        3180,
        400
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models/{{ $json._gemini_model }}:generateContent",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpQueryAuth",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({ contents: [{ parts: [{ text: $json._prompt }] }], generationConfig: { temperature: $json._temperature } }) }}",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 30000,
          "allowUnauthorizedCerts": false,
          "response": {
            "response": {
              "fullResponse": true
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "credentials": {
        "httpQueryAuth": {
          "id": "gemini_cred",
          "name": "Gemini API"
        }
      },
      "continueOnFail": true
    },
    {
      "id": "node_18",
      "name": "Check Gemini Response",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        3440,
        400
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "\nconst resp = $json;\nlet success = false;\nlet aiText = '';\ntry {\n  const statusCode = resp.statusCode || resp.$response?.statusCode || 0;\n  if (statusCode === 200 || resp.candidates) {\n    const candidates = resp.candidates || resp.data?.candidates;\n    if (candidates && candidates[0]?.content?.parts?.[0]?.text) {\n      aiText = candidates[0].content.parts[0].text;\n      success = true;\n    }\n  }\n} catch(e) { /* fail silently, will fallback */ }\nconst prev = $('Assemble Prompt').first().json;\nreturn {json: {...prev, _gemini_success: success, _ai_text: aiText, _raw_gemini: JSON.stringify(resp).substring(0,2000)}};\n",
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "node_19",
      "name": "IF Gemini OK",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        3700,
        400
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "combinator": "and"
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "g1",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json._gemini_success }}",
              "rightValue": true,
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "equals"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "node_20",
